  "slug": "hematopoietic-stem-identification-pre-4f51",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and publications pair single-cell transcriptomes with GWAS, eQTL and Mendelian randomization to nominate inflammatory disease genes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is integration of single-cell or cell-state data with bulk cohorts and genetic evidence, including GWAS, eQTL, Mendelian randomization and colocalization, to nominate candidate genes in inflammatory and immune-mediated disease. Myeloid and stromal compartments recur, including efferocytosis dysregulation in hidradenitis suppurativa lesional macrophages and a RAB20 myeloid hypothesis in otosclerosis, while THBS2-marked chondrocyte states and cholangiocyte subsets extend the pattern. What is comparatively new is layering genetic and regulatory evidence onto single-cell states, as in the atopic dermatitis and asthma study prioritizing shared regulatory genes with immune single-cell eQTLs and the lumbar spinal stenosis analysis linking GWAS signal to a stromal atlas. A contrasting result appears in ulcerative colitis trials, where a 200-gene mucosal score showed prognostic association while randomized treatment-by-score interaction evidence was limited. Most items remain candidate-level.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-18"
}
